linux-x86_64 seed, built from source at the commit named below (NOT the commit that
ships this file — the seed necessarily predates its own commit). Verified by
rebootstrap-linux.sh: LLVM-backend fixpoint + linux gate-full/gate-run + gate-cli +
gate-target-os. Needs libLLVM.so 21 (apt.llvm.org).

The seed embeds src/stdlib/*.coil via include-str at ITS build time, so a seed older than a
stdlib change cannot compile source that uses the new stdlib. Re-bless the seed in the
same commit as any src/stdlib/ change the compiler itself depends on, or the next clean
bootstrap breaks. `COIL_STDLIB_DIR=$PWD` can bridge an API-only stdlib change,
but cannot bridge syntax or representation changes the old compiler cannot parse.

