known host-specific gaps, NOT defects in this binary:
  * gate-cli's arm64 checks skip on Linux — the arm64 backend emits Mach-O, which
    GNU ld cannot read. They print a skip line naming the reason.
  * gate-ir and gate-diag stay macOS-only by design: gate-ir's corpus includes
    Objective-C, and gate-diag asserts macOS linker text.
  * The sanitizer checks need clang's runtime libs from the SAME llvm-config the
    compiler resolves — it uses `llvm-config --bindir`, not PATH, and CC= does
    not override it. Put the right bin first on PATH.
